invariant: INV-4
file: srv_auth.c
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_session
reason: sign_rsa_pss draws the RSA-PSS salt from ch_rand_bytes, the
  image's one generator, instead of the source the server's configuration
  names. Under RAND=session the signature would then not be a function of
  the session's stream, so a replay could not reproduce it. The session
  loop checks that the CertificateVerify signature is the one rsa_pss_sign
  computes over the server source's draw, and counts that draw.

--- old
    rand_draw(cfg, salt, sizeof salt);
--- new
    (void)cfg;
    void ch_rand_bytes(uint8_t *p, size_t n);
    ch_rand_bytes(salt, sizeof salt);
